Package: linux-image-7.3.0-2-aurora
Architecture: arm64
Depends: kmod, dracut, aura (>= 1.0.0~b12), aurora-audio, avd-fw, aurora-stage2-trial, aurora-userpages,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: firmware-linux-free
Provides: linux-image, wireguard-modules (= 1.0.0), aurora-ctxr-execmem
Description: Linux 7.3.0 for Apple Silicon Macs (Aurora)
 Aurora Silicon's shared kernel for Apple Silicon Macs: the image, modules and
 the Apple device trees (in /usr/lib/modules/<release>/dtb, with their DT ABI
 generation), which update-m1n1 composes into Stage 2.
 .
 It pairs with the pinned aura: an aura without the monitor needs this
 kernel's CTXR execution window (aurora-ctxr-execmem).

Package: linux-headers-7.3.0-2-aurora
Architecture: arm64
Build-Profiles: <!cross>
Depends: pahole, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Header files for Linux 7.3.0-2-aurora
 Headers, configuration and build scripts for building out-of-tree modules
 against the Aurora kernel 7.3.0-2-aurora.

Package: linux-image-aurora
Architecture: arm64
Depends: linux-image-7.3.0-2-aurora, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Aurora kernel for Apple Silicon Macs (latest)
 This package depends on the current Aurora kernel image, so that upgrades
 install new kernels alongside the running one.

Package: linux-headers-aurora
Architecture: arm64
Build-Profiles: <!cross>
Depends: linux-headers-7.3.0-2-aurora, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Header files for the latest Aurora kernel
 This package depends on the headers of the current Aurora kernel.

Package: aurora-userpages
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Run programs with 4K userspace pages on the Aurora kernel
 userpages 4k COMMAND runs a program, and the programs it starts, with 4K
 pages on the 16K kernel, for software that assumes 4K pages. It needs
 user4k=on on the kernel command line, which this package adds to GRUB's
 configuration unless /etc/default/grub already sets user4k=.
